
== 1. Rebuilding the script 45 comparison ======================
  melanoma (non-uveal): 56
  other lineages      : 940

== 2. Mann-Whitney recomputed from the rank statistic ==========
  Carrying the normal tail on the log scale so nothing underflows.
  'floor' is the smallest two-sided p these sample sizes could ever
  produce, i.e. under complete separation of the two groups.

  comparison                      n1    n2         z   |z|max     log10(p) floor log10(p)
  RASSF9 tss_proximal             56   940    +8.321    12.59       -16.06         -35.59
  RASSF9 shore                    56   940    -1.700    12.59        -1.05         -35.59
  RASSF9 distal                   56   940    +0.225    12.59        -0.08         -35.59
  RASSF9 core_minus_distal        56   940    +8.299    12.59       -15.98         -35.59
  RASSF10 tss_proximal            56   940    +2.067    12.59        -1.41         -35.59
  RASSF10 shore                   56   940    +6.599    12.59       -10.38         -35.59
  RASSF10 distal                  56   940    +1.495    12.59        -0.87         -35.59
  RASSF10 core_minus_distal       56   940    +1.321    12.59        -0.73         -35.59

  Reported in a defensible form:
    RASSF9 tss_proximal          p = 8.73e-17
                                   NOTE: wilcox.test returned exactly 0 here — underflow
    RASSF9 shore                 p = 8.91e-02
    RASSF9 distal                p = 8.22e-01
    RASSF9 core_minus_distal     p = 1.05e-16
                                   NOTE: wilcox.test returned exactly 0 here — underflow
    RASSF10 tss_proximal         p = 3.87e-02
    RASSF10 shore                p = 4.14e-11
    RASSF10 distal               p = 1.35e-01
    RASSF10 core_minus_distal    p = 1.87e-01

  INTERPRETATION OF THE FLOOR: no Mann-Whitney with these group sizes
  can return a p below the floor column, whatever the separation. Any
  smaller value quoted anywhere is an artefact and must be corrected.

== 3. Permutation cross-check ==================================
  Independent of any normal approximation. Resolution is 1/(2e+05+1); where no permutation is as extreme, the result is a BOUND.

    RASSF9 tss_proximal          observed shift +0.406 | 0 of 200000 permutations as extreme | p < 5.00e-06
    RASSF9 core_minus_distal     observed shift +0.264 | 0 of 200000 permutations as extreme | p < 5.00e-06
    RASSF9 distal (control)      observed shift +0.015 | 147067 of 200000 permutations as extreme | p = 7.35e-01

  The permutation test agrees in direction and significance but cannot
  resolve below ~5e-06 at this number of permutations. The normal
  approximation in section 2 is what supplies the exponent; the
  permutation result confirms it is not an artefact of that approximation.

